{title: 022 - God Is Our Song}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #022 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 22}
{meta: category Worship - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]God [C/G]is [Am]our [Bb]Song, [Am]and [Gm]every [F]singer [Bb]blest
[Dm]Who [F/C]praising [Am]Him [Gm]finds [F]energy and rest.
[C/E]All [F]who [Gm]praise God [Am]with [Gm]unaffected [C7/Bb]joy
[Am]Give [C/G]back [Am]to us [C]the [Bm]widom [Am]we [C/G]destroy,
[Am/E]Give back [F]to [Gm]us the [Am]widom [F]we [C/E]destroy.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]God [C/G]is [Am]our [Bb]Song, [Am]for [Gm]Jesus [C/E]comes [F/A]to [Bb]save;
[Dm]While [F/C]praising [Am]Him [Gm]we [F]offer all we have.
[C/E]New songs [F]we [Gm]sing, in [Am]ventures new [C]unite,
[Am]When [C/G]Jesus [Am/C]leads [C]us [Bm]upward [Am]into [F]light,
[Am/E]When Jesus [Gm]leads us [Am]upward [F]into light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]This [C/G]is [Am]our [Bb]Song [Gm]no [F]conflict ever [Bb]drowns;
[Dm]Who [F/C]praises [Am]God [Gm]our [F]human wrath disowns.
[C/E]Love [F]knows [Gm]what rich [Am]complexities [C]of [C7/Bb]sound
[Am]God [C/G]builds [Am]upon [C]a [Bm]simple [Am]common [F]ground,
[Am/E]God builds [F]upon [Gm/Bb]a [Am]simple [F]common ground.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F]God [C/G]is [Am]our [Bb]Silence [F]when no songs are [Bb]sung,
[Dm]When [F/C]ecstasy [Gm]or [F]sorrow stills the tongue.
[C/E]Glorious [Gm]the faith [Am]which [Gm]silently [C]obeys
[Am]Until we find [C]again the [Am]voice [C/G]of [F]praise,
[Am/E]Until [F]we [Gm]find again [F]the voice [C/E]of [F]praise.
{end_of_verse}
